{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-16239" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "In degrees, find the general solution to the equation $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}.$  Assume that $n$ is an integer." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994895/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c5cb48c3bc1fdc477acf79989c08dc7a8791214a0c99d053949e9a091403726"} {"question" "q-16239" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3})=-{30}^{∘}\n$$\n\nThe tangent function has a period of ${180}^{∘}.$  Hence, the general solution for the given equation is: \n\n$$\nx=-{30}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994895/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c5cb48c3bc1fdc477acf79989c08dc7a8791214a0c99d053949e9a091403726"} {"question" "q-16239" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994895/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "43210f3739d6bd5b2da149405301c1d4421939bcf8d5c668f19a61ecfe9073f4"} {"question" "q-16239" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994895/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c5cb48c3bc1fdc477acf79989c08dc7a8791214a0c99d053949e9a091403726"} {"question" "q-16239" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x=-{150}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘}"] ["math" "x=-{30}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘}"] ["math" "x=-{60}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘}"] ["math" "x={30}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘}"] ["math" "x={60}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994895/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c5cb48c3bc1fdc477acf79989c08dc7a8791214a0c99d053949e9a091403726"} {"question" "q-16239" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x=-{30}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994895/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c5cb48c3bc1fdc477acf79989c08dc7a8791214a0c99d053949e9a091403726"} {"question" "q-17339" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994895/assets/6839910f0269266caf6888e1e921506bd9585c6805e3d787538771cf379901f7.png)\n\nThe graph shows a portion of the curve $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ and $y=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.$ Which of the following generates the $x$-values of all of their points of intersection? Assume that $n$ is an integer." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994895/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c5cb48c3bc1fdc477acf79989c08dc7a8791214a0c99d053949e9a091403726"} {"question" "q-17339" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "At the intersection points, the $y$-values are the same for both graphs. This gives the equation $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.$ \n\nFirst, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})={30}^{∘}\n$$\n\nOur first solution lies in the $1$st quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}={30}^{∘}.$ Since $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x>0,$ the second solution must lie in the fourth quadrant, and it also has ${\\theta }_{R}={30}^{∘}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994895/assets/8c6e3ae6bdbfb1c66aee719f77225453992fffe6f3c6e3dfdc3f1ff92c59863a.png)\n\nSince the second solution ${x}_{2}$  lies in the $4$th quadrant, we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & ={360}^{∘}-{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & ={360}^{∘}-{30}^{∘} \\\\  & ={330}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the general solution for the given equation is\n\n$$\nx={30}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘},\\,x={330}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994895/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c5cb48c3bc1fdc477acf79989c08dc7a8791214a0c99d053949e9a091403726"} {"question" "q-17339" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994895/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "43210f3739d6bd5b2da149405301c1d4421939bcf8d5c668f19a61ecfe9073f4"} {"question" "q-17339" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994895/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c5cb48c3bc1fdc477acf79989c08dc7a8791214a0c99d053949e9a091403726"} {"question" "q-17339" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x={30}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘}"] ["math" "x={30}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘},\\,x={150}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘}"] ["math" "x={30}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘},\\,x={330}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘}"] ["math" "x={60}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘}"] ["math" "x={60}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘},\\,x={300}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994895/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c5cb48c3bc1fdc477acf79989c08dc7a8791214a0c99d053949e9a091403726"} {"question" "q-17339" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x={30}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘},\\,x={330}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994895/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c5cb48c3bc1fdc477acf79989c08dc7a8791214a0c99d053949e9a091403726"} {"question" "q-274744" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994895/assets/e4845bc1fbe702020161e15391e0c2bf8b8c2ee4fcd953790707ce5505d4df56.png)\n\nThe graph above shows a portion of the curve $y=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x$ and the line $y=2.$ The expressions \n\n$$\nx={\\theta }_{1}+n\\cdot b,\\,x={\\theta }_{2}+n\\cdot b,\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\theta }_{1}<{\\theta }_{2}$ and $n$ is an integer, generate the $x$-values of all of the points of intersection. Find the values of ${\\theta }_{1}$ and ${\\theta }_{2}$ in $[0,{360}^{∘}),$ and the value of $b.$\n\n${\\theta }_{1}=${{field-1}}${}^{∘},\\,{\\theta }_{2}=$\n{{field-2}}${}^{∘},\\,b=$\n{{field-3}}${}^{∘}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994895/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c5cb48c3bc1fdc477acf79989c08dc7a8791214a0c99d053949e9a091403726"} {"question" "q-274744" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "At the intersection points, the $y$-values are the same for both graphs. This gives the equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x},$ therefore the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{1}{2})={60}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nOur first solution lies in the $1$st quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}={60}^{∘}.$ Since $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x<0,$ the second solution must lie in the $4$th quadrant, and it also has ${\\theta }_{R}={60}^{∘}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994895/assets/40879eca8abd0b5b45d233a6aafe8642a10aaa7cf91b090bee86b47333beb0b8.png)\n\nSince the second solution ${x}_{2}$  lies in the $4$th quadrant, we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & ={360}^{∘}-{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & ={360}^{∘}-{60}^{∘} \\\\  & ={300}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe general solution for the given equation is \n\n$$\nx={60}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘},\\,x=-{60}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nWriting this as $x=\\theta +n\\cdot {360}^{∘},$ where $\\theta \\in [0,{360}^{∘}),$ we get\n\n$$\nx={60}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘},\\,x={300}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, since ${\\theta }_{1}<{\\theta }_{2},$ we have ${\\theta }_{1}=60\\,{\\,}^{∘},$ ${\\theta }_{2}=300\\,{\\,}^{∘},$ and $b=360\\,{\\,}^{∘}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994895/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c5cb48c3bc1fdc477acf79989c08dc7a8791214a0c99d053949e9a091403726"} {"question" "q-274744" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994895/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "43210f3739d6bd5b2da149405301c1d4421939bcf8d5c668f19a61ecfe9073f4"} {"question" "q-274744" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994895/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c5cb48c3bc1fdc477acf79989c08dc7a8791214a0c99d053949e9a091403726"} {"question" "q-274744" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "60"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994895/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c5cb48c3bc1fdc477acf79989c08dc7a8791214a0c99d053949e9a091403726"} {"question" "q-274744" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994895/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c5cb48c3bc1fdc477acf79989c08dc7a8791214a0c99d053949e9a091403726"} {"question" "q-274744" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "300"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994895/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c5cb48c3bc1fdc477acf79989c08dc7a8791214a0c99d053949e9a091403726"} {"question" "q-274744" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994895/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c5cb48c3bc1fdc477acf79989c08dc7a8791214a0c99d053949e9a091403726"} {"question" "q-274744" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "360"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994895/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c5cb48c3bc1fdc477acf79989c08dc7a8791214a0c99d053949e9a091403726"} {"question" "q-322666" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Assuming that $n$ is an integer, the general solution to the equation $3\\operatorname{csc}⁡x-6=0$ is given by \n\n$$\nx={\\theta }_{1}+bn,\\,x={\\theta }_{2}+bn,\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\theta }_{1}<{\\theta }_{2}.$ Find the values of ${\\theta }_{1}$ and ${\\theta }_{2}$ in $[0,2\\pi ),$ and the value of $b.$\n\n${\\theta }_{1}=${{field-1}}$,\\,{\\theta }_{2}=$\n{{field-2}}$,\\,b=$\n{{field-3}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994895/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c5cb48c3bc1fdc477acf79989c08dc7a8791214a0c99d053949e9a091403726"} {"question" "q-322666" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\,\\operatorname{csc}⁡x-6 & =0 \\\\ 3\\,\\operatorname{csc}⁡x & =6 \\\\ \\operatorname{csc}⁡x & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}.$ Therefore, the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=arcsin\\,(\\frac{1}{2})=\\frac{\\pi }{6}\n$$\n\nOur first solution lies in the $1$st quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}=\\frac{\\pi }{6}.$ Since $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x>0,$ the second solution must lie in the $2$nd quadrant, and it also has ${\\theta }_{R}=\\frac{\\pi }{6}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994895/assets/b0738a8a505b89ff687cb4de350a00f2e10d6209fbeee7dcdfdf0ee359a9cc3c.png)\n\nSince the second solution lies in the $2$nd quadrant, we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =\\pi -{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & =\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\pi }{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe general solution for the given equation is\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{\\pi }{6}+2\\pi n,\\,x=\\frac{5\\pi }{6}+2\\pi n.\n$$\n\nTherefore, since ${\\theta }_{1}<{\\theta }_{2},$ we have ${\\theta }_{1}=\\frac{\\pi }{6},\\text{ }{\\theta }_{2}=\\frac{5\\pi }{6},\\text{ }\\text{and}\\text{ }b=2\\pi .$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994895/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c5cb48c3bc1fdc477acf79989c08dc7a8791214a0c99d053949e9a091403726"} {"question" "q-322666" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994895/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "43210f3739d6bd5b2da149405301c1d4421939bcf8d5c668f19a61ecfe9073f4"} {"question" "q-322666" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994895/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c5cb48c3bc1fdc477acf79989c08dc7a8791214a0c99d053949e9a091403726"} {"question" "q-322666" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\pi}{6}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994895/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c5cb48c3bc1fdc477acf79989c08dc7a8791214a0c99d053949e9a091403726"} {"question" "q-322666" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994895/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c5cb48c3bc1fdc477acf79989c08dc7a8791214a0c99d053949e9a091403726"} {"question" "q-322666" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{5\\pi}{6}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994895/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c5cb48c3bc1fdc477acf79989c08dc7a8791214a0c99d053949e9a091403726"} {"question" "q-322666" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994895/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c5cb48c3bc1fdc477acf79989c08dc7a8791214a0c99d053949e9a091403726"} {"question" "q-322666" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2\\pi"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994895/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c5cb48c3bc1fdc477acf79989c08dc7a8791214a0c99d053949e9a091403726"} {"question" "q-323843" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the equation $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}+2}$ in the form $x=\\theta +n\\cdot b$ where $\\theta \\in [0,{180}^{∘}),$ $n$ is an integer and $b$ is the period in degrees.\n\n*Hint: You may use the fact that $tan\\,({75}^{∘})=\\sqrt{3}+2.$*\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘}+\\,n\\,\\cdot $\n{{field-2}}${}^{∘}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994895/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c5cb48c3bc1fdc477acf79989c08dc7a8791214a0c99d053949e9a091403726"} {"question" "q-323843" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}.$ Therefore, the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x} & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}+2} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =\\sqrt{3}+2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\sqrt{3}+2)={75}^{∘}\n$$\n\nThe tangent function has a period of ${180}^{∘}.$  Hence, the general solution for the given equation is\n\n$$\nx={75}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994895/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c5cb48c3bc1fdc477acf79989c08dc7a8791214a0c99d053949e9a091403726"} {"question" "q-323843" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994895/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "43210f3739d6bd5b2da149405301c1d4421939bcf8d5c668f19a61ecfe9073f4"} {"question" "q-323843" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994895/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c5cb48c3bc1fdc477acf79989c08dc7a8791214a0c99d053949e9a091403726"} {"question" "q-323843" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "75"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994895/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c5cb48c3bc1fdc477acf79989c08dc7a8791214a0c99d053949e9a091403726"} {"question" "q-323843" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994895/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c5cb48c3bc1fdc477acf79989c08dc7a8791214a0c99d053949e9a091403726"} {"question" "q-323843" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "180"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994895/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c5cb48c3bc1fdc477acf79989c08dc7a8791214a0c99d053949e9a091403726"}] "usage" {} "basis" 1058 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
